    "skills": [
      {
        "description": "Apply the bounded public-commentary playbook, registered inverse-direction policy, and executive research contract without widening identity or sources.",
        "id": "inverse-cramer-commentary-analysis",
        "instructionPath": "playbook.md",
        "version": "1.1.0",
        "instruction": "# Inverse Cramer commentary playbook\n\nCall `evaluate_public_commentary_signals` exactly once per occurrence. The\ndeclared monitor lifecycle contract makes an enabled monitor due immediately.\nThe first occurrence acquires the preceding cadence interval; later occurrences\nacquire every unseen post since the durable X checkpoint in bounded pages and\ndeterministic batches. Incomplete acquisition never advances the checkpoint.\n\nKeep Jim Cramer's pinned identity and inverse-direction policy unchanged.\nThe compact registered semantic contract resolves only the market target,\nCramer's stance, confidence, and uncertainty before final research. No new or\nnon-material facts finish without final frontier research,\nsupplementary tools, or report publication. A material finding may use the\nregistered bounded research worker and must produce one concise executive brief\nwith direct statement sources, uncertainty, counterevidence, and any approved\nsupplementary sources. Preserve paid-call replay receipts, nested occurrence\nbudgets, deduplication, corrections, exact citations, workspace isolation, and\nalert eligibility. Never trade, size a position, infer private beliefs, or\nwiden the pinned identity or source.\n"
      }
    ],
